I. INTRODUCTION

4D-BBS is a bulletin board program for the Amiga computer.  It
will allow you to run and maintain a public or private bulletin
board system accessible via a remote computer and modem.

4D-BBS contains all the standard features of a bulletin board
system along with a few extra's to set it apart from the others.

This program is intended for an experienced Amiga user, who has
dealt with telecommunications and knows how to operate AmigaDOS.

The BBS was written and organized by David R. Stromberger.
Message bases, private mail, and voting booth's programmed by
Dale E. Reed Jr.   Information about telecommunications, and some
bug fixes also by Dale.

This BBS is not in the public domain.  It is shareware, which
means that the programmers of this BBS, request that you send 
$25 dollars along with your mailing address.
When we have recieved your 25 dollar contribution, you will be
mailed a full working copy of the BBS.  Your name and address will
be cataloged so we can send you further upgrades to the BBS.
The demo version that you have now, is in fact, a full working 
copy of 4D-BBS.  The only thing that makes it a 'DEMO' is the
fact that before each menu prompt, the words 'DEMO COPY OF
4D-BBS' will be shown.  When you recieve your registered copy,
this will be removed.

